# Floe — Art assets

Floe's art is supplied with the project, under `assets/`. Seven folders cover the
critter, the bear, the three vehicles, and the two floes, and the build renders
each of those from its folder. Everything else the game shows is drawn in code,
and the last section of this file lists it.

## How the folders are organized

Each folder under `assets/` holds one PNG per frame, named by its frame index
(`0.png`, `1.png`, and so on). Every PNG has a transparent background in straight
alpha, so only its drawn pixels are opaque and each frame composites cleanly over
the ice and the water.

| Folder | Frames | Frame size | Spans | What it covers |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `assets/crosser/` | `CROSSER_FRAMES` (`8`), `0`–`7` | 32 x 32 | 1 tile | The critter |
| `assets/bear/` | `BEAR_FRAMES` (`18`), `0`–`17` | 32 x 32 | 1 tile | The bear, running, swimming, and lunging |
| `assets/plow/` | `PLOW_FRAMES` (`1`), `0` | 96 x 32 | 3 tiles | The snow plow |
| `assets/dogsled/` | `DOGSLED_FRAMES` (`1`), `0` | 64 x 32 | 2 tiles | The dogsled |
| `assets/car/` | `CAR_FRAMES` (`1`), `0` | 64 x 32 | 2 tiles | The car |
| `assets/pan/` | `PAN_FRAMES` (`1`), `0` | 32 x 32 | 1 tile | The one-tile floe |
| `assets/raft/` | `RAFT_FRAMES` (`2`), `0`–`1` | 128 x 32 | 3 or 4 tiles | The long floes |

Frame sizes are in pixels of source art, `SPRITE_TILE` (`32`) to a tile. A tile
is `TILE` (`32`) logical units square, so a 32 x 32 frame maps onto one tile at a
scale of one.

## How they are drawn

- A 32 x 32 frame is drawn over one tile, centered on its subject's own center,
  so the critter and a bear are drawn where `specs/strait.md`'s map puts them.
- A lane item's frame is drawn `32` units wide for every tile the item spans,
  with its left edge on the item's own `x` and its top on its row's top edge: a
  plow `PLOW_W` (`96`) units wide over its three tiles, a dogsled `DOGSLED_W`
  (`64`) and a car `CAR_W` (`64`) over their two, a one-tile floe `PAN_W` (`32`)
  over its one. `RAFT_W` (`128`) is the width of the raft art itself.
- The three-tile raft is the left `96 x 32` of `assets/raft/0.png`, drawn over its
  three tiles. The four-tile raft is the whole of `assets/raft/1.png`, drawn over
  its four tiles. A long floe reads as one continuous slab rather than as small
  floes butted together.
- Each vehicle's art faces right. A vehicle in a lane whose `dir` is `-1` is drawn
  mirrored horizontally, so every vehicle faces the way its lane runs. The bear
  and the floes are never mirrored, the bear because it carries a frame set per
  facing.
- The sprites are pixel art, and they stay crisp at every scale the stage is
  fitted to.

Where a frame set holds two frames for a state, alternate them while the subject
is in that state, at a rate that reads as motion. The rate is yours.

## How they are loaded

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The build loads the frames itself. Every URL it requests resolves against the
page rather than against the origin root, so the produced site runs unchanged
whether it is served from the root of a static host or mounted under a sub-path.
The produced site is self-contained and carries every frame it draws.
{{else}}
The {{engine.name}} engine provides the asset loader, documented in the `engine/`
directory at the root of this repository. It resolves every path under one root,
`assets/`, relative to the page the build is served from, and it fetches and
decodes the file. The build loads each frame through that loader rather than
requesting a URL of its own, writing the path relative to that root:
`bear/0.png`, `raft/1.png`.

The produced site serves every seeded frame under that root, so a path the loader
resolves reaches the seeded file at whatever base path the site is served from.
{{/if}}

## The critter: `assets/crosser/`

Eight frames, a two-frame crouch-and-leap pair for each of the four facings.

| Frames | Facing |
| --- | --- |
| `0`, `1` | down |
| `2`, `3` | up |
| `4`, `5` | left |
| `6`, `7` | right |

Draw the critter from the pair for its current facing, which
`specs/hopping.md` fixes. A critter resting in a filled bay, and a lives icon in
the HUD, may reuse one of these frames.

## The bear: `assets/bear/`

Eighteen frames, all top-down: a four-facing run, a four-facing submerged swim,
and a lunge.

| Frames | Set | Facing |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `0`, `1` | Run | down |
| `2`, `3` | Run | up |
| `4`, `5` | Run | left |
| `6`, `7` | Run | right |
| `8`, `9` | Swim | down |
| `10`, `11` | Swim | up |
| `12`, `13` | Swim | left |
| `14`, `15` | Swim | right |
| `16`, `17` | Lunge | any |

| The bear is | Drawn from |
| --- | --- |
| Travelling on ice footing | The run pair for its facing |
| Swimming | The swim pair for its facing |
| Catching the critter | The lunge frames |

A catch is drawn from the lunge pair at the point on the strait where the bear
and the critter met, on the tick the catch happens and for as long as the hold
that follows it runs. It is drawn there although no bear is on the strait over
that hold, because a catch takes every bear off it: `specs/hunter.md` and
`specs/progression.md` fix that.

The swim frames already carry the submerged silhouette and its wake, so a bear
over the water stays trackable, including where it passes under a floe.
`specs/hunter.md` fixes when a bear is swimming.

## The vehicles: `assets/plow/`, `assets/dogsled/`, `assets/car/`

One frame each, drawn at the widths above over the tiles the vehicle spans.
`specs/ice.md` fixes which lane carries which.

## The floes: `assets/pan/` and `assets/raft/`

`assets/pan/0.png` is the one-tile floe. `assets/raft/` carries the long floes:
frame `0` is the three-tile raft, drawn in the left `96 x 32` of the image with
its right tile transparent, and frame `1` is the four-tile raft, filling the
whole `128 x 32`. `specs/water.md` fixes which lane carries which.

## What is drawn in code

No folder covers the following. Each is rendered by the build, and the spec named
beside it fixes its behavior.

| Drawn in code | Fixed by |
| --- | --- |
| The strait itself: the water, the ice of the shores, the median and the ice band, and the far shore | `specs/strait.md` |
| The bays, open and filled | `specs/bays.md` |
| The bonus catch | `specs/bays.md` |
| The HUD, every screen, every menu, and all text | `specs/ui.md` |
| The debug overlay | `specs/instrumentation.md` |
